browned:
All the dog-wood blossoms are underneath the tree,
Browned at the edges, turned in a day;
And I would with all my heart they trimmed a mound for me,

bronze:
As worth an artist’s study for the folds,
As that bronze opposite! nay, the bronze has faults;
Art’s here too artful,—conscious as a maid,

broom:
Snatch of me your pleasure,
Where the broom-straw marks the leaf;
Women quiet with your weeping

brooks:
All the strength of his manly prime;
Nor music of birds, nor brooks, nor bees,
Was as sweet as the dollar's chime.

brow:
That Love at length should find me out and bring
This fierce and trivial brow unto the dust,
Is, after all, I must confess, but just;

She hangs like a star in the dew of our song;
She springs like a beam on the brow of the tide,
She falls like a tear from the eyes of a bride.

broadening:
Sporting at ease and courting full in view.
When loftier still a broadening darkness flew,
Down-swooping, and a ravenous hawk revealed;

brooches:
Who own the ample sea;
Or brooches, when the Emperor
With rubies pelteth me;

brood:
My treasure ad my heart store Thou in Thee,
Brood over me with yearnings of a dove;
Be Husband, Brother, closest Friend to me;

broomstick:
Must melt down golden pieces in the nard
Wherewith to anoint her broomstick ere she rides;
And poets evermore are scant of gold,

brook's:
I wound myself in a white cocoon of singing,
All day long in the brook’s uneven bed,
Measuring out my soul in a mucous thread;

And there's a hill across the brook,
And down the brook's another;
But, oh, the little hill they took,--

Measuring out my soul in a mucous thread;
Dimly now to the brook’s green bottom clinging,
Men behold me, a worm spun-out and dead,

broadcloth:
Scares muslin souls away;
If broadcloth breasts are firmer
Than those of organdy,

broidered:
That misbecame them in a holy place,
With broidered hems of perfumed handkerchiefs;
Those passed the salts with confidence of eyes

Or may be slept too late;
With eaglets broidered on his cap,
And eaglets on his glove?

broadclof:
An' dat one ol' squeaky fiddle soun' to you jes' lak a ban';
Cotton britches look lak broadclof an' a linsey dress look fine,
When Angelina Johnson comes a-swingin' down de line.

browsing:
To the tinkling bells
Of the brown sheep browsing;
Sailors crying through the storm;

brooked:
And a shaking, sharp, suspicious way;
His blinking eyes had scarcely brooked
The light of day.
